findings.detail:
**Why the flash is gone.** The player is the victim, so the localized flash goes to its contact at the head. That is behind the lens and hidden in first person, and 0.25 m doesn't reach the visible arms or guard fists. Before phase 3 the arms flashed white.

**What a clean hit on the player now shows:**
- a light burst about 3-4% of the view wide, placed straight ahead at the lens (comic_sprite.gd:108-124), so at screen centre over the attacker's face;
- the HP bar drop with its white ghost (HUD);
- about 3 px of shake;
- the guard dropping, if it was raised;
- on close sparring jabs, the attacker's forearm as a long brown spike from the bottom-left to the view centre for 5 frames, then a one-frame snap when _pull_strike pulls it back after hitstop.

**The confusion.** The burst is the same white light star, in the same place, as a jab the player lands on that face. With the guard down, nothing on screen tells taking a hit from giving one, except the HUD bar.

**Known item (a) verdict:** reads weakly. Same picture in combo's 'Flank hit lands' (with the guard up, the fists drop) and in the hold-break jab.

In combo_bot side-view captures, the log panel covers about x 0.58-0.98 and y 0.46-0.68 of the frame, right beside the player. The struck body flies or falls into exactly that area in every side-view act, and the panel's translucency leaves only a dim shape:
- the P P P P launch (legs under it);
- the spinning backfist and the K K K spinning heel (body fully under it);
- the haymaker;
- the flying kick (lying body under it);
- the spin kick (the right-hand dummy under it for the whole act);
- the throw and the flying body (both dummies under it);
- every hold-view side act (the held body's back).

In first person the same panel covers right-side contacts: the front kick's light burst draws gray under it (combo.avi f903-908), and so does part of the pipe smash's burst. The side-view impact frame also turns the panel white.

No input toggles the log in play (grab-03).
